  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">to Support Disaster Preparedness and Food Assistance for Flood Affected Vulnerable Households (JAMUNA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of the Anticipatory Action framework for floods in Bangladesh and aims to provide multi-purpose cash assistance to vulnerable people to be affected by floods in the district of Bogra, Jamalpur, Gaibandha, Kurigram, and Sirajgani. This WFP project provides unconditional cash assistance to 378,500 people of whom 127,290 are women, 92,089 are men, and 159,121 are children. 6,045 people with disabilities are also targeted under this project.</narrative>
  </description>
